ation  [Music]  this method of protection is already  used by more than 37 of american users  if you like me post your videos on  youtube then you already know exactly  what this is  two-factor authentication is based on  the fact that it's simply not enough to  simply know the correct password to log  in you've also got to have some kind of  pre-arranged item to hand be it an email  address a mobile phone number right and  in fact your bank card works in the same  way  the pin code is the key that you know  and the card itself is the key that you  own right if you're an accountant or the  owner of a company you've probably  encountered security keys or tokens  before these are often confused with  ordinary flash drives but actually a  unique key is stored inside them which  cannot be copied and can be used as the  second factor of authentication now in  2017 google conducted an experiment on  its employees 85 000 people received a  ub key security key and for a year  hackers were unable to get access to any  of the protected accounts now unlike sim  cards they cannot be cloned and unlike a  mailbox they cannot be lured out by  phishing  the only drawback of these keys is the  price the most affordable ub key costs  about 25 us dollars i think this is one  of the factors preventing these tokens  from being widely used  the good news is that with such a key we  can completely abandon inconvenient  passwords  [Music]  look we already have keys in our hands  that are difficult to forge or steal  unnoticed so why bother with passwords  at all  many have thought about it but microsoft  managed to take the first big step  towards this idea in september 2021  windows users were able to delete  passwords 85 million people logged in  using windows hello or the microsoft  authenticator looks like a lot of people  are getting bored with passwords for  passwordless authentication we can use  one or a couple of factors from the  classic three let's weigh the advantages  and disa